usage: slack_chat_react.py [-h] [--session SESSION] [--current]
                           [--conversation-id CONVERSATION_ID]
                           [--message-id MESSAGE_ID] [--emoji EMOJI]
                           [--remove]

Add an emoji reaction to the latest inbound Slack message for this session, or
to an explicit (channel, ts) pair.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --session SESSION     Override session id; claims that session's identity
                        for ingestion proof
  --current             React on the latest inbound message routed to this
                        session (resolved via gc transcript). This is the
                        default — pass it for clarity or omit it; if
                        --conversation-id is given, explicit mode wins.
  --conversation-id CONVERSATION_ID
                        Slack channel id (explicit mode; requires --message-
                        id).
  --message-id MESSAGE_ID
                        Slack message ts (explicit mode; requires
                        --conversation-id).
  --emoji EMOJI         Emoji name without colons (default: eyes).
  --remove              Remove the reaction instead of adding it (adapter maps
                        this to Slack reactions.remove).
